<title>USA: Cooper Industries Inc Q1 shr increases.</title>
<headline>Cooper Industries Inc Q1 shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Call mean estimate for Q1 was $0.62 per share.</p>
<p>				1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.71		    $0.58</p>
<p> Shr diluted		 0.67		     0.56</p>
<p> Net			 77,700		   62,100</p>
<p> Revs		   1,318,900		1,291,700</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     110,053		  107,389</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     124,327		  124,166</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - Fully diluted share amounts assume conversion of the 7.05 percent convertible subordinated debentures to common stock. As a result, interest on the debentures - $5.7 million in 1997 and $7.3 million in 1996 - was added back to net income in the computation of fully diluted earnings per share.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
